{"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SignalBatchStrategy"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"text":"Signal","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Signal","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Signal","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci","text":"AsyncSequence","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The signal’s elements are ignored; only their arrival counts. Use it with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","type":"reference"},{"text":" or a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/CurrentValueSubject","type":"reference"},{"text":" to flush on demand. A value already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"available at subscription, such as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"CurrentValueSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s current value, fires when the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signal’s task subscribes. That task starts alongside the upstream’s, so elements may already","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have arrived and the first batch may be short. A signal that finishes stops firing and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batches go on until the upstream finishes; a signal that throws ends the batched sequence with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its error, except ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" while the batched sequence is still running (a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SingleValueSubject","type":"reference"},{"text":" someone else cancelled): then the signal stops firing and the batches go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Example","anchor":"Example","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let flush = PassthroughSubject<Void>()","for try await lines in logLines.batch(strategy: .signal(flush)) {","    write(lines)","}","\/\/ Elsewhere, when the app moves to the background:","flush.send()"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SignalBatchStrategy"}],"platforms":[{"name":"iOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false},{"name":"iPadOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false},{"name":"macOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false},{"name":"tvOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","unavailable":false},{"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","unavailable":false},{"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"9.0","unavailable":false}],"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"SignalBatchStrategy","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SignalBatchStrategy"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:7Afluent19SignalBatchStrategyV","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Afluent"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SignalBatchStrategy.swift","url":"https:\/\/gith